{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_22916abf5c50d08ac92b0f56e6f60002200e80c9147cdda686877440656a4818"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI is distributed as routa-cli on npm and crates.io, with commands such as routa --help, routa acp list, and routa workspace list."},{"claim_ids":["clm_38a6d9c7056885d8526445cbb1fb0b6aafbaa10f2cc8c884805403277a8bbfeb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The implementation is intentionally dual-backend: a Next.js web app in src/, a Tauri desktop shell backed by an Axum server in crates/routa-server, sharing semantics defined by api-contract.yaml."},{"claim_ids":["clm_57d083d4ae653f8acbbbe7de9eaa2400a2a87243c6aee1c97555ee073279f11d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Built-in lane prompts live under resources/specialists/workflows/kanban/*.yaml, and core role prompts (routa, crafter, gate) under resources/specialists/core/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5ee473c51bfe5e67818cdde7ebbe30a87126f3433c6b2d4e37c533a57556b84c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Routa is described as a workspace-first multi-agent coordination platform for software delivery, keeping goals, tasks, sessions, traces, evidence, and review state visible on a board rather than in one chat thread."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6490c16d69edc7484e597dc3cf3403030a9a20783b848c953a1669955b758e5d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Work flows through Kanban lanes Backlog, Todo, Dev, Review, Done, each backed by a specialist prompt (Backlog Refiner, Todo Orchestrator, Dev Crafter, Review Guard, Done Reporter), with a Blocked Resolver for blocked work."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cac67e64e405953ff060de1a04427ac8c3a78ae6608a1d73bd2708a48ef0f881"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each downstream lane is deliberately stricter than the previous one; cards accumulate artifacts (story YAML, execution brief, dev evidence, review verdict, completion summary) as they move forward."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cd8623e22d4b5467b9d32111b6fb11424b31d8a09601ae0199645abfff5ddc2b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository map includes crates/routa-core (shared Rust runtime foundation), crates/routa-cli (CLI entrypoints and ACP serving), and crates/harness-monitor (run observation and operator-facing harness monitor)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d11b0ec7559c88ef159c25f0445fa0562d4e978d624bdc1668358fac7f975d08"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Integration surfaces listed include ACP, MCP, A2A, AG-UI, A2UI, REST, and SSE."},{"claim_ids":["clm_df0add6a4692c86d54c96c19f328dd61f4469d558a075367d6c3ec3c471980df"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Badges indicate TypeScript 5.9, Next.js 16.2, and Rust with Axum; the project is MIT licensed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ee5e3b746d38d78181ea6990be01595949421d4a1d729363f5cd049499a23f54"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The review gate is a stacked decision path with three layers: Harness Monitor (what happened), Entrix Fitness (what should be true, hard gates and evidence requirements), and Gate Specialist (whether the card can move)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_22916abf5c50d08ac92b0f56e6f60002200e80c9147cdda686877440656a4818","clm_38a6d9c7056885d8526445cbb1fb0b6aafbaa10f2cc8c884805403277a8bbfeb","clm_57d083d4ae653f8acbbbe7de9eaa2400a2a87243c6aee1c97555ee073279f11d","clm_5ee473c51bfe5e67818cdde7ebbe30a87126f3433c6b2d4e37c533a57556b84c","clm_6490c16d69edc7484e597dc3cf3403030a9a20783b848c953a1669955b758e5d","clm_cac67e64e405953ff060de1a04427ac8c3a78ae6608a1d73bd2708a48ef0f881","clm_cd8623e22d4b5467b9d32111b6fb11424b31d8a09601ae0199645abfff5ddc2b","clm_d11b0ec7559c88ef159c25f0445fa0562d4e978d624bdc1668358fac7f975d08","clm_df0add6a4692c86d54c96c19f328dd61f4469d558a075367d6c3ec3c471980df","clm_ee5e3b746d38d78181ea6990be01595949421d4a1d729363f5cd049499a23f54"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:31:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_a5c9b1a4fdd54c2a8ddc30641f47a109","id":"pg_3c0e366c0272504ba5270231ad9c3f11","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/phodal-routa-readme-md-e48861ab81e2-0231ad9c3f11.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_780a01174d315d5284553833bdc171eb"],"title":"phodal/routa/README.md @ e48861ab81e2","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:31:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a5c9b1a4fdd54c2a8ddc30641f47a109"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_34a75e150c9bc04939dbbc2d67eda5a741d7e21963d839e501db193a6c732e2f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: commits must follow Conventional Commits with one concern per commit, under 10 files and 1000 changed lines, exactly one co-author line, and UI PRs should include screenshots or recordings."},{"claim_ids":["clm_952115dfe6cd75f7ad3c372b404ec9c77686c9fc4d1eddd72194dcdbf59750c2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors must run entrix validation before PR using docs/fitness/README.md as the canonical rulebook, with tiers fast and normal, and build via cargo build -p entrix."}],"claim_ids":["clm_34a75e150c9bc04939dbbc2d67eda5a741d7e21963d839e501db193a6c732e2f","clm_952115dfe6cd75f7ad3c372b404ec9c77686c9fc4d1eddd72194dcdbf59750c2"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:31:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_a5c9b1a4fdd54c2a8ddc30641f47a109","id":"pg_901b8cbd87155309a356253a44d9b614","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/phodal-routa-agents-md-e48861ab81e2-253a44d9b614.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_5ceeb15a367f5a01adbcb07f88794305"],"title":"phodal/routa/AGENTS.md @ e48861ab81e2","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:31:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a5c9b1a4fdd54c2a8ddc30641f47a109"}
